.TH FIP 1 "2026-07-13" "fipindicateur" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fip, fipindicateur \- system-tray client and command line for FIP webradios
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fipindicateur
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B fip
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fipindicateur
is a small system-tray client for the FIP (Radio France) webradios on Linux
(GNOME/X11 is the supported target).
.PP
Run with no argument,
.B fipindicateur
launches the tray icon and its menu. The same binary also acts as a command
line: control subcommands talk to an already-running instance over a local
socket and exit, so playback can be driven from scripts and keybindings.
.PP
The
.B fip
name (installed as a symlink to the binary) is the command-line front end. It
.I never
launches the tray: run with no argument it prints the current status
(equivalent to
.BR "fip status" ).
An unknown subcommand prints usage and exits 2. When invoked as
.BR fipindicateur ,
an unknown first argument likewise prints usage and exits 2 rather than
launching the tray.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the current playback state as a single JSON line (station, playing,
artist, title, show, volume, mute, version).
.TP
.B play
Start playback.
.TP
.B pause
Pause playback.
.TP
.B toggle
Toggle between play and pause.
.TP
.BI "station " id
Switch to the webradio with the given identifier. Unknown identifiers are
rejected. See
.B stations
for the list.
.TP
.B stations
List the known webradio identifiers, one per line.
.TP
.BR "stats " [ \-\-out " " \fIfile.html\fR ] " " [ \-\-no\-open ]
Build the local listening report as a self-contained offline HTML page and
open it in the browser.
.B \-\-out
writes the report to the given file instead of a temporary one;
.B \-\-no\-open
suppresses opening the browser. Reads only the local opt-in event log; nothing
is sent over the network.
.TP
.BR "cast " [ scan ]
Scan the local network for Chromecast devices (mDNS) and list them, one per
line (friendly name, address:port). Runs standalone, without a running
instance.
.B cast
alone behaves as
.BR "cast scan" .
.TP
.B version
Print the build version and exit.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit 0.
.PP
The
.BR status ", " play ", " pause ", " toggle ", " station " and " stations
commands require a running instance. With none running they print
.I fipindicateur n'est pas lanc\['e]
to standard error and exit 1.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/fipindicateur.sock
Control socket exposed by the running instance (mode 0600, per user). Falls
back to the system temporary directory when
.I XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is unset. Removed on a clean shutdown; a stale node from a crash is cleared on
the next launch.
.TP
.I ~/.config/fipindicateur/config.json
Persisted settings (station, volume, mute, and the opt-in toggles).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/fipindicateur/events.jsonl
Opt-in local listening event log (play, pause, station changes, volume). Off
by default; written only after the user enables the local statistics option.
Records behaviour, never track identity. This is the file the
.B stats
report reads.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/fipindicateur/history.jsonl
Opt-in track-change log (artist and title). A separate consent and a separate
file from the event log. Both logs are append-only JSON, one object per line,
local only, and can be inspected or deleted by hand.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
.PP
Project documentation and source: the repository's README, docs/INSTALL.md and
docs/FEATURES.md.
